  "body": "**Filed by the pool-quota steward (149th run, 2026-11-04T13:30Z) from the quota gatherer's Turso leg — the surge flagged in the steward ledger at the 147th and 148th runs has accelerated and now has a filing of its own, per the file-the-issue rule.**\n\n## Measured series (hub `quota-current.json`, source openchamber-quota, Turso leg)\n\n| Run | Tick (UTC) | Storage | Rows written | Rows read / mo |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 147th | 2026-11-04T11:15Z | 3.463348 GB (69.3%) | 148,184 | — |\n| 148th | 2026-11-04T12:15Z | 3.866595 GB (77.332%) | 191,940 (+43,756) | 411,185,113 (82.237%) |\n| 149th | 2026-11-04T13:15Z | 4.342985 GB (86.860%) | 247,467 (+55,527) | 413,260,794 (82.652%, +2,075,681) |\n\n- Storage grew **+0.476 GB in the last hour** (vs +0.403 GB the hour before). At the current pace the 5 GB free-tier storage cap binds in **~1.4 hours**; even at half pace it binds today, 2026-11-04.\n- Rows-read is at 82.652% of the 500M monthly cap with the cycle resetting Dec 1 — it binds later than storage at current pace, but it is the second wall in line.\n- Databases 3/100 — not the constraint. The growth is in one mirrored dataset's storage + write volume, not database count.\n\n## What is needed\n\n1. Identify the writer(s) driving ~55k rows-written/hour and ~0.48 GB/hour of storage growth in the Turso mirror (which table(s), which sync/producer).\n2. Decide the remedy: prune/compact the mirror, slow or scope the sync, or raise the Turso plan — a plan change is Drew's call (money); the steward does not change plans, funds, or credentials.\n3. Until then the steward keeps reporting the Turso leg hourly in the pool-change ledger; the board attention items already surface \"Turso — Storage 87%\" and \"Turso — Rows read / month 83%\".\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- The growth source is named (table + producer), and either the growth rate drops back inside the free-tier caps with headroom to the Dec 1 cycle reset, or a plan decision is recorded here.\n",
